{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5hbhEgTqpSiSeHrKhJG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a POST endpoint `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, allows idempotent retries on already-confirmed shipments, rejects `CANCELLED` shipments with HTTP 409, and rejects unknown shipments with HTTP 404.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model with ShipmentStatus enum at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- ShipmentController at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` (currently has create, getById, list but no confirm)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` with save() method that persists updates\n- Error handling via ApiException hierarchy at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-31` with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` centralizes error response wrapping\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler wraps them in ApiError envelope\n2. Endpoints return `ResponseEntity<T>` with explicit HttpStatus (CREATED for 201, no status = 200)\n3. Repository methods (save, findById, etc.) are thin wrappers around in-memory state\n4. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath matchers; every error test asserts both status and error body\n5. Comments explain intent (e.g., Shipment.kt:6-7 notes this baseline has no way to move shipments)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add ErrorCode for shipment state conflicts (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or similar) to support 409 on CANCELLED\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add POST `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, retry on CONFIRMED, reject CANCELLED, reject unknown\n\n**Risks:**\n- Concurrency: the in-memory store uses ConcurrentHashMap, which is safe for read-modify-write of shipment status\n- Test isolation: tests must reset repository in @BeforeEach (already done)\n- Breaking change: adding an ErrorCode is additive and safe; throwing ConflictException on CANCELLED is the only new error path\n\n**Open questions:**\n- The requirement does not name the ErrorCode for the CANCELLED shipment case. I will add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to signal that the shipment is in an invalid state for the confirm operation. This mirrors the pattern of status-based conflicts rather than uniqueness conflicts (like SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS).\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum to distinguish state conflicts (shipment is CANCELLED) from existence conflicts (shipment already exists or doesn't exist).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   - Fetch the shipment via `repository.findById(shipmentId)` \n   - If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, ...)`\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent retry)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED via `repository.save(shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED))`\n   - Return the updated shipment with 200 OK (default ResponseEntity behavior)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment and returns it`: create S-1, confirm S-1, assert status is CONFIRMED and 200 OK\n   - `allows a retry and returns the already-CONFIRMED shipment unchanged`: create S-2, confirm twice, both return CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error code`: manually insert CANCELLED shipment into repository, confirm, assert 409 and SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirming an unknown shipment with 404`: confirm non-existent S-999, assert 404 and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could add a `ConfirmShipmentRequest` DTO to document intent, but the endpoint takes no body parameters (shipmentId is in URL). A request body is unnecessary and would violate REST semantics.\n- Could modify the repository to return the old and new shipment separately, but `save()` already returns the persisted shipment, which is the standard pattern.\n- Could throw a different exception type for state conflicts, but ConflictException (409) is the correct status for both uniqueness and state conflicts, and the ErrorCode distinguishes them.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Code |\n|------|------|-------|----------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 Shipment | OK |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | findById(id) | (no write) | 200 Shipment | OK |\n| CANCELLED | findById(id) | (no write) | 409 ApiError | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| Unknown id | findById(id) returns null | (no write) | 404 ApiError | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **Test 1**: \"confirms a created shipment\" — verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and persistence (POST, 200, status field)\n- **Test 2**: \"allows retry on confirmed shipment\" — verifies idempotence: two POS Ts both return 200 and CONFIRMED (no error)\n- **Test 3**: \"rejects cancelled shipment\" — verifies state guard: insert CANCELLED directly via repo, POST, assert 409 + SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n- **Test 4**: \"rejects unknown shipment\" — verifies lookup: POST to non-existent id, assert 404 + SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me now implement the changes. First, I'll add the error code to ApiError.kt:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2241,"cache_read_input_tokens":15981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2241},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61837eee-2dad-483e-bb63-2d342d0a41d3","uuid":"c585b3f0-f83a-425b-8e7c-2346453310dc","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:30:31.557Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5hbgmuStdqChhEWRMUU"}
